# This repository sets core.autocrlf = true, because the working tree is
# edited on Windows and a LF/CRLF mismatch once made `git status` report
# 4505 modified files when 70 were real.
#
# Line-ending conversion applied to a BINARY file corrupts it, silently and
# completely. Git normally avoids that by guessing: a file with a NUL byte
# near its start is treated as binary. Guessing is the wrong mechanism for
# a shipped boot image, so the binaries this repository carries say what
# they are instead of relying on it.
#
# -text means: never convert line endings, in either direction.

*.img   -text
*.bin   -text
*.blb   -text
*.dat   -text
*.dtb   -text
*.elf   -text
*.png   -text
*.pdf   -text
*.clm_blob -text
*.MOD   -text
*.pmf   -text

# A checksum list is read by sha256sum -c, which takes a carriage return as part
# of the file name. It must reach every checkout with LF endings, Windows included.
SHA256SUMS text eol=lf
